From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: the CPU decode of a trimmed texture reads and decodes only the kept mip levels (EDEN_UP_DECODE_KEPT_LEVELS), off by default

What: with EDEN_NX2_TEX_TRIM_MIB the host keeps an image without its top mip levels
(host_level_offset != 0), but QueueAsyncDecode (texture_cache.h) still unswizzled the whole guest
image into its input and sized the output for every level (MapSizeBytes), though the dropped levels
are never decoded or uploaded. At the first 3D scene the two 1365x1365x90 ASTC arrays asked for
214 + 107 MiB of output and 2 x 54 MiB of input while the pool fell to 32 MiB. With mode 2 the guest
is read from the first kept level's offset (FullUploadSwizzles(info)[skip].buffer_offset), the input
is CalculateUnswizzledSizeBytes(info, skip), UnswizzleImage runs with first_level = skip (as
UploadLayers does), and the output is sized to the kept levels' converted layout. The copies name
the same guest levels and, after ConvertImage, are identical to today's; both upload paths read the
kept levels from offset 0 as before. For these two arrays: input 53.75 -> 13.60 MiB each, output
214.38 -> 53.75 and 107.19 -> 26.88 MiB, 321.25 MiB in all (281 MiB the most at one moment). Only
2D images with host_level_offset != 0 on the asynchronous CPU decode are affected.

Switch (one digit, read once in the TextureCache constructor): EDEN_UP_DECODE_KEPT_LEVELS: 1 count
only (sizes as before), 2 act, 3 verify for a test run (the old way decodes and uploads; the kept
levels are also read, unswizzled and decoded the new way and inputs, copies and outputs compared
byte for byte); unset, 0 or anything else off.
Log: boot (stderr) "EDEN_UP_DECODE_KEPT_LEVELS=N: asynchronous decodes of trimmed images counted
only (sizes as before)|read, unswizzle and decode only the kept levels|verified (old way used, new
way compared)"; per trimmed decode (HW_GPU Info, first 16 then powers of two)
"EDEN_UP_DECODE_KEPT_LEVELS first: trimmed decode of 0x... WxHxL (N levels, format F) from level S:
input X -> Y MiB, output X -> Y MiB (applied)|(count only, sizes as before)|(verify: old way
used)|(verify: old way, not compared) (n so far)"; every 10 s while on (stderr, from
TickAsyncDecode) "EDEN_UP_DECODE_KEPT_LEVELS 10s: mode M, trimmed decodes N, input X MiB and output
Y MiB not allocated|would not be|(verify), held Z MiB less now (peak P), verified V, differ D";
verify mismatches (HW_GPU Warning, first 8) "EDEN_UP_DECODE_KEPT_LEVELS verify: the kept levels'
input of 0x... (...) differs from the old one" and "... the kept levels' decode of a WxHxL image
differs from the old one".

Not in TranslationSwitches: only CPU buffer sizes on the decode thread change; the host image and
the bytes uploaded into it are the same (what =3 checks), so no shader or pipeline input moves.

Cost when off: one static int test per decode and per frame (TickAsyncDecode); each queued decode
task is 64 bytes larger (four empty captures) and each decode context 8 bytes; every size, the guest
read, UnswizzleImage(..., 0), out_size and the zero fill are today's to the byte.

Default flip (later, after the cold =1/=2 runs and a =3 run with differ 0): in DecodeKeptLevelsMode
(texture_cache.h) "if (value == nullptr) return 2;" before the digit check ("0" still turns it off).

Risks: util.h documents UnswizzleImage's first_level "for an image of one layer"; the 90-layer use
is correct by the arithmetic (layer stride from the full layer size) and the =3 run proves it on
real data. =3 costs the kept input and output once more per trimmed decode plus a second guest-read
copy (about 54 MiB) on the GPU thread; verify on a warm start. The guest-read copy
(swizzle_data_buffer) barely shrinks (only layer 0's level 0 is skipped).

Composes with 0584 (EDEN_UP_TEX_TRIM_2D): 0584 does not touch texture_cache.h; it only gives single
2D ASTC textures a host_level_offset (vk_texture_cache.cpp TrimmedHostInfo), and this change reads
host_level_offset, so with both on a 2D texture that 0584 trims and that goes to the CPU async
decode is decoded kept-levels-only too (the 6144x6144 ground texture: input 30.75 -> 7.70, output
48 -> 12 MiB). 0584 off or its CHECK=1: nothing trimmed, nothing here either.

Origin and credit: our own. Draft drafts-2026-11-11/ports-7/first-start/decode-kept-levels/draft.diff
(made on T132, review verdict ready to place, no code change asked), placed unchanged; every hunk
applied at an offset of 1 or 3 lines (0588's include and Beat() lines), no context changed.
